WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.288
A keyframe is a saved value at one moment in time.

2
00:00:02.288 --> 00:00:05.033
The yellow diamond says: at this moment, the square is here.

3
00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:07.000
Nothing moves until there are at least two.

4
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.563
Add a second keyframe later in time and change the value.

5
00:00:10.563 --> 00:00:13.563
The tool animates everything in between for you.

6
00:00:13.563 --> 00:00:15.000
Two diamonds, one move.

7
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.278
Each property has its own row of keyframes.

8
00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:23.000
Scale up from a little smaller and fade in while it moves, and the entrance feels richer than a plain slide.

9
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.161
By default most tools move at a constant speed.

10
00:00:25.161 --> 00:00:31.000
Choose an easing for the keyframes, usually ease in-out or ease out, and the curve bends so the motion starts and stops gently.
